# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. Vendor licences forbid redistribution, and none of it is source.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The directory patterns are anchored to the repository root with a leading
# slash, and they must stay that way.
#
# An unanchored "data/" matches at any depth, so it also matches alpha/data/.
# That is not hypothetical: it silently excluded the entire alpha/data package
# from every commit early in this project. The package existed on disk, the
# README referenced it, the tests imported it and passed, and git said
# nothing. The gap only appears on a fresh clone, by which point the history
# that should have contained the package does not.
#
# That failure has the shape this whole pipeline is built to guard against.
# It is silent, and it fails in the flattering direction: everything local
# keeps working, so nothing prompts anyone to look. Anchoring is the fix, and
# tests/test_repository.py asserts both halves of it, that no data file is
# tracked and that every source file is.
/data/
/cache/
/runs/
/scratch/

*.parquet
*.npz
*.csv

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The registry and the pool. See docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md: these are the asset.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials. Never a file, always the environment. See alpha/config.py.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebooks. A notebook embeds its output cells, so a head() of vendor data
# or a printed key becomes a committed artefact that no diff review catches,
# because nobody reads a JSON blob of base64. If one is ever wanted it goes
# in /scratch/, which is ignored above.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.ipynb

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Noise
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so

.venv/
venv/
env/

build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.numba_cache/
.benchmarks/

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
